### Theorem OC.1

Let \(\lambda>1\). Under (OC.1)--(OC.3), if
\[
\boxed{
\sigma>
\frac{\operatorname{area}C}{a_0}\left(1-\frac1{\lambda^2}\right)
+\frac{D}{a_0\lambda}
+\frac{\operatorname{per}C}{2}+2,
}
\tag{OC.4}
\]
then such an exterior cap cannot occur in \(A\).

Equivalently, every surviving contact-minimal source satisfies
\[
\boxed{
\sigma\le
\frac{\operatorname{area}C}{a_0}\left(1-\frac1{\lambda^2}\right)
+\frac{D}{a_0\lambda}
+\frac{\operatorname{per}C}{2}+2.
}
\tag{OC.5}
\]

The additional geometric loss is \(D/(a_0\lambda)\), not
\(\operatorname{per}(C)/(a_0\lambda)\).

There is also an exact section-profile version. Write
\[
\ell_C(t)=\mathcal H^1\bigl(C\cap\{x:u\cdot x=c+t\}\bigr),
\qquad
b_\lambda(C,u)=\int_0^\lambda \ell_C(t)\,dt,
\tag{OC.4a}
\]
where \(\ell_C(t)=0\) beyond the cap height. Then the same proof gives the
stronger sufficient condition
\[
\boxed{
\sigma>
\frac{\operatorname{area}C}{a_0}\left(1-\frac1{\lambda^2}\right)
\;+\;
\frac{b_\lambda(C,u)}{a_0\lambda^2}
\;+\;
\frac{\operatorname{per}C}{2}+2.
}
\tag{OC.4b}
\]
Indeed \(b_\lambda(C,u)=\operatorname{area}(C\setminus U_\lambda)\), and
\(b_\lambda(C,u)\le\lambda\operatorname{diam}C\le\lambda D\), so (OC.4)
is the uniform corollary of (OC.4b).

### Theorem EA — external-annulus capacity

Let \(K\) and \(F\) be compact convex planar sets with \(F\subseteq K\), and let
\(X\subseteq K\setminus F\) be a finite set with pairwise distances at least one.
Then

\[
\boxed{
|X|\frac{\pi}{4}
\le
\operatorname{area}(K)-\operatorname{area}(F)
 +\frac12\bigl(\operatorname{per}K+\operatorname{per}F\bigr)
 +\frac\pi4.
}
\tag{EA.2}
\]

In particular, if both sets have diameter at most \(D\), then

\[
\boxed{
|X|\le \frac4\pi\bigl(\operatorname{area}(K)-\operatorname{area}(F)\bigr)+4D+1.
}
\tag{EA.3}
\]

### Theorem AS.1 — exact two-sided annular population squeeze

Every post-ZF C-II survivor satisfies

\[
\boxed{
\frac2{\sqrt3}A_{ann}-\frac12\operatorname{per}F
< Z_{ext}
\le
\frac2{\sqrt3}
\left(A_{ann}+\operatorname{per}K+\operatorname{per}F+\pi\right).
}
\tag{AS.7}
\]

Consequently, uniformly over every unbounded survivor sequence,

\[
\boxed{
Z_{ext}
=\frac2{\sqrt3}A_{ann}+O(D).
}
\tag{AS.8}
\]

### Theorem ZX.1 — finite external rattler floor

Every post-ZF C65 survivor satisfies

\[
\boxed{
Z_{ext}
\ge
n-
rac{2h^2}{\pi\sqrt3}-h-1.
}
\tag{ZX.1}
\]

